# addresses.json and addresses.*.json are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# They are this repo's record of which contracts are deployed, and ignoring
# them made that record exist only on whichever laptop last ran a deploy: a
# fresh clone had no address book at all, no CI anywhere could compare against
# one, and the authoritative copy was one disk failure from being recoverable
# only by reading it back out of a downstream copy in the backend's
# .env.example.
#
# Nothing in them is secret. Contract ids are public on-chain identifiers, the
# admin field is a public G-address, and every value is already committed to
# README.md here and to .env.example, README.md, onchain-details.tsx and
# lib/api.test.ts in the other two repos — so ignoring them protected nothing
# and hid the one copy that is supposed to be canonical.
#
# scripts/deploy_testnet.sh writes these files, so a redeploy now produces a
# diff. That is the point: a deployment that changes a contract id should
# leave a commit saying so.
.env